# MoneyRight needs no settings to run. Copy to .env.local only to change these.

# Tailnet logins allowed to reach the app at all, comma-separated. Anyone else
# on the tailnet gets a 403 before they see the sign-in page. Empty means any
# tailnet member (they still need a MoneyRight account).
# MONEYRIGHT_ALLOWED_LOGINS=you@example.com,partner@example.com

# Where the database and encryption key live. Defaults to .moneyright/<env>/
# in this repo, kept apart for dev and production.
# MONEYRIGHT_DATA_DIR=/path/to/dir

# The 32-byte encryption key, base64. Normally generated on first run into
# the data directory; set it here only to keep it somewhere else.
# MONEYRIGHT_MASTER_KEY=

# --- Linking accounts --------------------------------------------------------
# This app's own credentials with Plaid, shared by every MoneyRight
# user. Each person's bank tokens are sealed in the database, never here.
# Keep this file owner-only: chmod 600 .env.local
#
# The dev server reads .env.development.local instead, so it can use
# sandbox keys while production uses real ones.

# Plaid (https://dashboard.plaid.com) — banks, cards, brokerages, loans. The
# Trial plan allows 10 production Items for life.
# PLAID_CLIENT_ID=
# PLAID_SECRET=
# sandbox | production. Default: sandbox.
# PLAID_ENV=sandbox

# --- Backups -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the nightly encrypted backups go. Default: .moneyright/backups/<env>,
# on the same disk as the database — set this to somewhere that leaves this
# Mac, e.g. a folder in iCloud Drive:
# MONEYRIGHT_BACKUP_DIR="/Users/you/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/MoneyRight Backups"
# Restoring needs master.key (from .moneyright/production/), which must NOT
# be kept beside the backups — put a copy in your password manager.
